  "final_message": "I restored `channel`, but I couldn't confirm the result. The test run finished with exit code 0, but I couldn't read its output because reading the output file was denied. I haven't run the real ARCH-4 check, because its contract isn't in this repo.\n\n**Why CI failed:** `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). So my earlier removal broke a consumer that does read the field, and my first answer wrongly said nothing did.\n\n**The fix:** I put `channel` back everywhere I had removed it:\n- The `Order` and `NewOrder` types, the `CHANNELS` constant and its validation in `src/core/order.ts`.\n- The `OrderPlaced` event and its builder in `src/core/events.ts`.\n- Request parsing in `src/api/requestParsing.ts`.\n- The `createApp` example in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n- The test fixtures and assertions.\n\n`git diff` against HEAD shows only `channel` additions plus the test lines that check for it. HEAD itself doesn't include `channel`, so the removal had already been committed. The working-tree changes are what bring it back, and they still need to be committed.\n\n**Still to do:** Run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run arch` yourself, or re-run CI. If `channel` should really go, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, bump the event's `schemaVersion` to 4.",
